  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains several programs (Associate of Arts in Business intro only, BA Instructional Design, BA Liberal Arts, and a truncated BA Marketing); this ledger assumes BA Instructional Design was intended. Confirm the target program.",
    "EDU 100 satisfies 3 credits of Global Campus Foundations requirements, but the capture does not say which specific Foundations course it replaces; listed items sum to 123 credits with this 3-credit overlap (33 + 39 + 51 - 3 = 120).",
    "GEN 101 is scheduled as the first course and counts toward 3 elective credits; the capture does not state whether it is mandatory within the 51 elective credits, so it is not listed separately.",
    "Bachelor students transferring fewer than 30 credits must take GEN 104 (3 elective credits); this conditional requirement is not itemized.",
    "The capture states Foundations courses may be substituted but does not list approved substitutions.",
    "Residency: a minimum of 30 credits must be completed at the University, but no specific courses are designated as institution-only.",
    "Upper-division: a minimum of 30 upper-division credits, including 18 upper-division credits in the major, is required; the capture does not define which course levels count as upper-division.",
    "Minimum cumulative GPA of 2.00 in all coursework attempted at the University is required for graduation."
  ],
